# Pointing Recording Developer Handoff

## Scope and source of truth

- Canonical repository: the repository containing this file.
- Delivery branch: `feat/integrated-vr-interactions-recording`.
- Unity project: `signvr_unity/`, Unity `6000.5.6f1`.
- Host project: `vr-sign-host/` (FastAPI + React).
- Runtime scene: `signvr_unity/Assets/Scenes/VRroom.unity`.
- Requirement source: `E:\SignVR_Unity\有指代数据录制细节.pdf`.
- Exact 31-row mapping and authored world coordinates:
  `POINTING_SENTENCE_CATALOG.md`.

The live Unity Editor may be opened on `E:\SignVR_Unity`; it is a working mirror.
Commit and push only the canonical `VR-Sign-Record-System` repository, and keep
shared Unity code/scene files byte-identical between the two trees.

## Recording contract

The dataset has exactly 31 sentences:

| Viewpoint | Sentences | Rule |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `state_01` | 3 | One of three boxes |
| `state_02` | 9 | Cartesian product of three coins and three plates |
| `state_03` | 3 | One of three picture frames |
| `state_04` | 3 | One of three keys |
| `state_05` | 7 | Every non-empty subset of exactly three buttons |
| `state_06` | 6 | Every permutation of exactly three breakers |

The state-5 buttons are only `industrial_button`, `red_button`, and
`alarm_button`. `elevator_button_-_lift` is not a target. The state-6 breakers
are the three `free_switch_handler_ue5` roots. Do not convert either group into
seven physical objects.

Repeated HMD prompt text is intentional. The referent changes through visual
highlighting. `target_label` is host-only context that lets the supervisor
distinguish entries such as `按钮 A+C` or `电闸顺序 B→C→A`.

## Runtime ownership

| Component | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `RecordingRuntimeBootstrap` | Installs the recording stack only for `VRroom`; it keeps the authored XR rig and scene. |
| `RecordingCoordinator` | Owns countdown, recording, finalization, reset, pause handling, and completion events. |
| `RecordingSentenceSequence` | Holds the Inspector-editable 31 entries and mirrors host selection by `sentence_id`. |
| `RecordingPointingSentenceCatalog` | Provides the canonical Unity defaults used by the scene configurator and validation. |
| `RecordingViewpointController` | Aligns the tracked XR view to one of six disabled world-space reference cameras. |
| `RecordingViewpointSceneStateController` | Opens the safe in `state_02`, opens both closet doors in `state_05/06`, and restores closed poses elsewhere. |
| `RecordingTargetPoseLock` | Keeps all catalog targets at authored poses and disables physics/grab movement. |
| `RecordingPointingTargetController` | Resolves target paths only when the sentence changes and feeds cached transforms to the cue renderer. |
| `RecordingTargetVisualCues` | Draws subtle pulsing bounds outlines; state 6 also displays floating `1/2/3` labels. |
| `RecordingIndexFingerRays` | Draws both index-tip rays from real hand skeletons and reports target-bound hits without colliders. |
| `RecordingHandSkeletonVisualizer` | Reuses the main tracked hand joints and displays a per-bone skeleton instead of the hand mesh. |
| `RecordingPromptBubble` | Renders the rounded, depth-independent upper-left prompt bubble. |
| `MetaBodyMotionRecorder` | Writes 30 Hz pose JSONL and atomic metadata with quality gates. |
| `QuestDeviceGateway` | Pairs with the host and applies host-authoritative recording and `select_sentence` commands. |
| `QuestTakeUploader` | Uploads completed real-pose artifacts and preserves unacknowledged local files. |
| `vr-sign-host` | Owns batches, rounds, sentence selection, foot-pedal input, external video, and final disk layout. |

The architecture intentionally has one bootstrap and one recording state machine.
Static authored data lives in the sentence catalog/scene. Mutable capture state
lives in the coordinator. Presentation components subscribe to sequence and state
events; they do not poll or search the scene every frame.

## State and advancement

```text
Ready -> Countdown -> Recording -> Finalizing -> Completed
  ^          |                         |
  |          +-- short press ----------+
  |             cancel, no artifact
  +-- reset/invalid Take: retain or restore the intended sentence
```

- A normal stop finishes the Take, advances the host cursor by one, and sends a
  follow-up `select_sentence` command to Quest.
- Quest queues selection received during `Finalizing`/`Resetting` and applies it
  on return to `Ready`/`Completed`.
- A countdown cancellation releases the reserved empty Take and does not advance.
- A long press after a completed Take returns to the sentence just recorded and
  allocates a new Take ID. Existing files are never overwritten.
- Too-short, invalid-pose, paused, passthrough-interrupted, capture-error, or
  I/O-error Takes do not advance.

## Controls

No Touch controller or Quest OS button is part of the recording protocol.

| Action | Input |
| --- | --- |
| Start / cancel countdown / stop | Short `Space` in the focused host page |
| Re-record previous/current sentence | Hold `Space` for 1.2 seconds |
| Previous / next sentence | Host `Left Arrow` / `Right Arrow`, page buttons, list click, or numeric jump |
| Recorder inside Quest | Uses the USB HID foot pedal mapped to `Space`; no in-VR sentence/scene controls |

The foot pedal connects to the host PC and emits keyboard input into the focused
browser. The supervisor alone selects sentence and scene. Quest and host only
need to share the trusted LAN; the pedal does not pair with Quest.

The obsolete in-headset previous/next hand panel and Quest-to-host
`sentence_offset` signal were removed. Do not reintroduce them without changing
the recording protocol and supervisor workflow.

## Visual cue timing

- During `Ready`, targets and finger rays are hidden.
- During `Countdown` and `Recording`, every target for the current sentence gets
  a subtle cyan bounds outline. A coin/plate sentence highlights both objects;
  a state-5 sentence highlights the selected non-empty button subset.
- In state 6 all three breakers are outlined. Floating numbers are assigned to
  each breaker according to that sentence's permutation.
- Both index rays start at `Hand_IndexTip`, use `Hand_Index3 -> Hand_IndexTip`
  as direction, and turn green when intersecting an active target Bounds.
- Bounds, labels, and ray hits do not require target colliders. This is required
  because recording props are deliberately collision-free.

The bounds approach avoids changing shared materials. Several targets share a
material, so mutating `sharedMaterial` would highlight unrelated objects.

## Fixed props and deterministic doors

Every unique target in the 31-sentence catalog is a fixed visual reference.
Scene configuration and runtime startup both enforce the contract:

- Rigidbody: Kinematic, no gravity, no collision detection, all axes frozen.
- `Grabbable`: disabled.
- Authored local position/rotation/scale: restored late each frame as a guard
  against third-party interaction scripts.

`state_02` opens `safe/.../Object_5` around its left edge by `105°`.
`state_05` and `state_06` open both `closet/.../RootNode/LeftDoor` and
`RightDoor` around generated outer-edge hinges by `+105°` and `-105°`.
All transitions first restore exact authored closed poses, so repeated switching
does not accumulate transform drift. There is no interaction or animation.

## World frame

- OVR tracking origin is `FloorLevel`.
- `resetTrackerOnLoad` and `AllowRecenter` are disabled.
- Selecting a sentence aligns the XR rig so the current tracked head reaches the
  authored reference-camera eye position. Height differences do not redefine
  target world coordinates.
- `VRPlayerRig` and `RecordingModeController` suppress locomotion, player-root
  drift, XR-origin recalibration, and recorder collisions while leaving tracked
  head rotation and both hands live.
- Metadata records `world_frame_id=VRroom-world-v1`, viewpoint pose, actual
  XR/head pose, floor Y, alignment error, tracking origin, and correction count.

Reference cameras must stay disabled in Android builds. `CenterEyeAnchor` is the
only `MainCamera` and the only Quest render camera.

## Catalog synchronization

The same ordered 31 entries are authored in:

1. `RecordingSentenceSequence` on `VRroom/RecordingViewpoints`.
2. `vr-sign-host/backend/app/pointing_sentence_catalog.json`.

Keep these fields synchronized:

```text
sentence_id, zero-based index, text, viewpoint_id,
target_label, highlight_target_ids, sequence_numbers
```

Run `Tools/SignVR/Configure Pointing Recording` after changing Unity defaults.
It rewrites the scene sequence, freezes target physics, creates missing door
hinges, saves the scene, and runs validation. Never reuse an existing round after
changing catalog length/order. The old 300-sentence catalog remains available as
`vr-sign-host/backend/app/sentence_catalog.json` for the other dataset.

## Artifact and network contract

Quest/local output:

```text
Application.persistentDataPath/Recordings/{session}/{sentence}/
  {stem}.pose.jsonl
  {stem}.meta.json
  {stem}.meta.json.uploaded
```

Host output:

```text
{data_root}/{batch_id}/{round_id}/{sentence_id}/{take_id}/
  {take_id}.pose.jsonl
  {take_id}.meta.json
  {take_id}.camera.webm
```

| Port | Protocol | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 8000 | HTTP / WebSocket | Operator UI, uploads, preview |
| 5005 | UDP | Device announcement, ACK, live pose |
| 5006 | UDP | Quest discovery and host commands |

Editor-simulated artifacts contain `editor_simulation=true` and
`pose_source_simulated=true`; they stay local and the host rejects them. A real
completed Quest Take requires at least 15 frames and at least 90% valid pose
frames.

## Local development

Open `signvr_unity/Assets/Scenes/VRroom.unity`, then run:

```text
Tools/SignVR/Configure VRroom Player and Physics
Tools/SignVR/Configure Pointing Recording
Tools/SignVR/Validate VRroom Player and Physics
Tools/SignVR/Validate Pointing Recording
```

Host setup and run:

```powershell
cd vr-sign-host/backend
py -3.12 -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements-lock.txt

cd ../frontend
pnpm install
pnpm build

cd ..
.\scripts\start-local.ps1
```

Operator console: `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.

## Required validation before push

```powershell
cd vr-sign-host/backend
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q

cd ../frontend
pnpm lint
pnpm build

cd ../../
git diff --check
```

Also verify:

- Unity compiles with zero errors.
- `Validate Pointing Recording` reports 31 sentences, six viewpoints, all target
  paths resolved, fixed target physics, deterministic safe/closet doors, and one
  XR render camera.
- State 5 has seven and only seven button subsets.
- State 6 has six and only six breaker permutations with visible `1/2/3` labels.
- Editor simulation shows the rounded prompt, target outline, skeleton, and two
  index rays without overlap or blank rendering.
- An Android build installs and launches on Quest 3; the host can pair, select a
  sentence, start/stop a Take, and receive Pose/Meta.

## Extension rules

- Do not add another recording state machine, XR camera rig, or per-frame scene
  search.
- Add presentation behavior through coordinator/sequence events.
- Preserve every existing candidate Take; retake allocates a new ID.
- Update Unity defaults, scene, host JSON, tests, coordinate table, and this handoff
  together when the catalog changes.
- Keep generated data, station config, virtual environments, frontend builds,
  Unity `Library/Temp/Logs`, screenshots, and APK output out of Git.
